Rāvaṇa bids hiding Sītā love him without fear --- Rāvaṇa cites rākṣasa law yet vows never to force unwilling Sītā --- Rāvaṇa urges her to shed braid dirt and fast for jewels and pleasures --- Rāvaṇa praises unmatched beauty and fleeting youth and offers chief queenship --- Rāvaṇa boasts none match him and mocks bark-clad Rāma as fallen perhaps dead --- Rāvaṇa bids her rule his harem and sport in seashore groves
